@startuml gui_class
title plogic - GUI

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class GUI {
  +{static} should_launch(argv: List<OsString>): bool
  +{static} run(): Result
}

class PlogicApp {
  -input: str
  -simplify: bool
  -show_table: bool
  -show_process: bool
  -outcome: Outcome?
  -cursor: CCursorRange?
  +evaluate()
  +insert_at_cursor(ctx: &Context, text: str)
  +delete_before_caret(ctx: &Context)
  +cursor_bounds(): (int, int)
  +set_caret(ctx: &Context, index: int)
  +remember_cursor(cursor: CCursorRange?)
}

class View {
  +assessments: List<Assessment>
  +show_table: bool
  +show_process: bool
}

enum Outcome {
  Evaluations(View)
  Errors(List<str>)
}

class Orchestrator

class Assessment {
  +formula: str
  +variables: int
  +simplification: Simplification?
  +table: TruthTable?
}

class TruthTable

class Simplification {
  +expression: Expression
  +steps: List<Step>
}

class Step {
  +rule: Rule
  +expression: Expression
}

note bottom of PlogicApp
  The whole window is one vertical scroll area. Header,
  input section and centered result components flow in the
  same column, with no separate result pane (ADR-051). The
  help is a collapsed one-column-set list at a smaller
  size. All three modes are snapshotted in View when
  Evaluar is pressed; changing one afterwards only affects
  the next evaluation. Mostrar tabla off calls assess with
  no table; on, assess builds only below ten variables. No
  table means no classification (ADR-049).

  The toolbar inserts a connective at the remembered
  caret and offers variable, borrar and Limpiar. borrar
  deletes the selection when there is one, otherwise the
  character before the caret; insertion and deletion share
  cursor_bounds and set_caret (ADR-055).
end note

GUI ..> PlogicApp : <<create>>
PlogicApp --> Outcome
Outcome --> View
View --> Assessment
PlogicApp ..> Orchestrator : assess(source, simplify, max_variables)
Assessment --> TruthTable
Assessment --> Simplification
Simplification --> Step : steps

@enduml
